.TH ROPCOLLISION 1
.SH NAME
ropcollision \- drawing a sprite to ask what it would have hit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/ropcollision
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ropcollision
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Collision.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
It is a different program from
.B Demo/Games/Collision.HC,
which is ported as
.IR collision (1).
.PP
One sprite follows the pointer and one sits in the middle of the window.
The demonstration is the raster operation
.BR ROP_COLLISION ,
which draws nothing: it walks the pixels the sprite would have set and
counts each one that is already something other than the background
colour.  So the centre sprite is drawn twice a frame, once invisibly to
ask what it would have landed on, and once for real \- in a second,
taller shape if the answer was anything at all.  The running count is
printed at the left of the window.
.PP
Because the test is the sprite's own pixels rather than its bounding box,
a shape can be moved through a hole in another shape without ever
registering a hit.
.PP
This tree has no such raster operation, so the frame is composed
offscreen and the centre sprite's mask is walked against it, in the
original's order: the pointer sprite is already drawn when the question
is asked, and the count is printed afterwards, so the text can never
contribute to it.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "the pointer"
Move the first sprite
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/ropcollision.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR collision (1),
.IR wm (1)
